A long plan in one session: eight small functions, each with a test, planned
as todos and done one after another. Each todo is entered with mem.Next()
and popped with its result, so the session's context stays near its size at
the start instead of growing with every function, and the plan ends closed.

-- project/go.mod --
module strutil

go 1.22
-- project/strutil.go --
// Package strutil has small string helpers.
package strutil
-- prompt --
Add these eight functions to strutil.go, each with its own test in strutil_test.go: Reverse(s string) string (by runes), IsPalindrome(s string) bool (ignoring case), CountVowels(s string) int, TitleCase(s string) string, Truncate(s string, n int) string (n runes at most), PadLeft(s string, n int) string (spaces), PadRight(s string, n int) string (spaces), and Words(s string) []string (split on whitespace). Plan them as todos in mem and work through all of them, running the tests as you go.
-- check --
turn 1 tool gnovm_run >= 9
cmd go test ./...
cmd for f in Reverse IsPalindrome CountVowels TitleCase Truncate PadLeft PadRight Words; do grep -q "func $f(" strutil.go || exit 1; grep -q "func Test$f" strutil_test.go || exit 1; done
mem-count done >= 9
mem-count open == 0
